{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463180",
      "title": "Data Binding + Event Binding = Two-Way Binding",
      "lectureOrder": 29,
      "videoOrder": 25,
      "sourceHash": "845038a4a9edb21c62665ab29fae3be80b1920aebb51f7959d8d640b34169a06",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.82,
          "en": "So back in the project worked on before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.82,
          "end": 8.92,
          "en": "A bit simplified, I dumped the event modifiers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.92,
          "end": 12.5,
          "en": "I dumped v-ons and you find this snapshot attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.5,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "to this lecture in case you all don't want to start from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "well, this state again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 19.29,
          "en": "So I'm back in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.29,
          "end": 21.9,
          "en": "where we have this input element that the buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 23.933,
          "en": "for the counter and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.07,
          "end": 29.67,
          "en": "Now let's say our goal is to have another button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.67,
          "end": 33.74,
          "en": "maybe here below the input where we say resetInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.76,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "And the buttons should do what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 41.223,
          "en": "It should reset the input in, well, the input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 45.36,
          "en": "For that, we can add a new method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.36,
          "end": 48.71,
          "en": "resetInput, or however you wanna name it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.71,
          "end": 52.69,
          "en": "And in there, how do we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.69,
          "end": 56.4,
          "en": "In there we now want to be clear this input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.4,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "Now we could try to get access to the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 64.7,
          "en": "through JavaScript with document.querySelector, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.66,
          "end": 67.68,
          "en": "get access to the input like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 71.453,
          "en": "access to value property and set it to an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.44,
          "end": 76.44,
          "en": "This might actually work, but it's very hacky.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.44,
          "end": 79.99,
          "en": "We're not using Vue to then fall back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.99,
          "end": 82.98,
          "en": "to such explicit JavaScript instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.98,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "That's not the idea behind using Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 87.67,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna stay in the Vue world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.67,
          "end": 90.553,
          "en": "and leverage Vue and its features for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.39,
          "end": 93.64,
          "en": "So how could we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.64,
          "end": 98.64,
          "en": "Well, we could use the name, data property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.34,
          "end": 103.25999999999999,
          "en": "which is the value we're ultimately updating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.25999999999999,
          "end": 104.97,
          "en": "on every key stroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 109.75,
          "en": "And output it here in input by setting value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.75,
          "end": 113.25999999999999,
          "en": "the value attribute equal to name, however, not like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.25999999999999,
          "end": 117.39,
          "en": "but instead since name is dynamic and managed by Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 119.273,
          "en": "with help of v-bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.28,
          "end": 125.28,
          "en": "With that I'm making sure that name is reflected here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.74,
          "end": 128.9,
          "en": "So this name here is reflected in the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.9,
          "end": 130.66,
          "en": "Why am I doing that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.66,
          "end": 134.02,
          "en": "Well if I now go to resetInput",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 134.02,
          "end": 137.05,
          "en": "and set this name equal to an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.05,
          "end": 141.01,
          "en": "that empty value should be reflected in the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.01,
          "end": 145,
          "en": "and we should be able to set it back to an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 145,
          "end": 147.11,
          "en": "Now we'll have one problem with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.11,
          "end": 149.97,
          "en": "And that is that in set name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.97,
          "end": 152.9,
          "en": "I'm not setting name to just what the user enters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.9,
          "end": 156.98,
          "en": "but to what the user enters plus the last name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.98,
          "end": 159.53,
          "en": "And that would lead to a strange behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 159.53,
          "end": 162.59,
          "en": "if we then reflect name back into this input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.59,
          "end": 164.05,
          "en": "I can actually show it to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.05,
          "end": 168.01,
          "en": "If I reload you'll see if I start typing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.01,
          "end": 170.85,
          "en": "Schwartzmueller gets added over and over again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.85,
          "end": 172.69,
          "en": "which is not the idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.69,
          "end": 175.96,
          "en": "So for the moment, let's get rid of this last name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.96,
          "end": 177.4,
          "en": "which we add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.4,
          "end": 180.25,
          "en": "And let's just store what the user enters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.25,
          "end": 182.68,
          "en": "with every keystroke in name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.68,
          "end": 185.7,
          "en": "and then reflect named back into the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.7,
          "end": 189.23,
          "en": "so that there we really reflect what the user entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.23,
          "end": 194.04,
          "en": "And now let's also connect this button here with v-on:click",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.00900000000001,
          "end": 199.01,
          "en": "to this newly added resetInput method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.01,
          "end": 200.24,
          "en": "so that this is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.24,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "when the resetInput button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 204.63,
          "en": "And with that, if I now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.63,
          "end": 207.4,
          "en": "I can enter Max here and it all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.4,
          "end": 210.95,
          "en": "But if I click resetInput, we cleared it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.95,
          "end": 213.21,
          "en": "We also cleared in the paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 216.57999999999998,
          "en": "because there we're referring to the same name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.57999999999998,
          "end": 218.39,
          "en": "which we reset here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.39,
          "end": 220.66,
          "en": "but that's just a little side effect here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.66,
          "end": 222.79,
          "en": "Of course if you wanted to prevent that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.79,
          "end": 225.51,
          "en": "we could use a separate value, which would be output here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.51,
          "end": 229.2,
          "en": "which be confirmed upon hitting enter or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.2,
          "end": 233.2,
          "en": "I showed this before, how we could work with two values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.2,
          "end": 235.43,
          "en": "confirmed input and irregular input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 235.43,
          "end": 237.76,
          "en": "but that's not what this is about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.76,
          "end": 240.92,
          "en": "Instead, what this is about is about the fact that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.92,
          "end": 243.97,
          "en": "this is a pattern you could need in some occasions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.97,
          "end": 247.46,
          "en": "You might have inputs where you don't just want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.46,
          "end": 250.22,
          "en": "to get the value the user entered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.22,
          "end": 254.17,
          "en": "but where you also want to set the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.17,
          "end": 256.79,
          "en": "of the input so that you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.79,
          "end": 259.99,
          "en": "can reset it with a button or any other logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.99,
          "end": 262.13,
          "en": "you have on your page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.13,
          "end": 264.03,
          "en": "And you can then achieve this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.03,
          "end": 266.22,
          "en": "by not just listening to the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 266.22,
          "end": 270.79,
          "en": "but by also sending the stored value back into the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.79,
          "end": 272.9,
          "en": "by binding the value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.9,
          "end": 275.69,
          "en": "This is a common pattern you could need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.69,
          "end": 277.84000000000003,
          "en": "And actually it's so common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.84000000000003,
          "end": 279.56,
          "en": "that you need something like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.56,
          "end": 283.22,
          "en": "that Vue has a shortcut for this you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.22,
          "end": 287.36,
          "en": "It has a special built in directive which simplifies this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.36,
          "end": 292.36,
          "en": "If you bind the value and listen to input changes on input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.44,
          "end": 296.27,
          "en": "you can get rid of all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.27,
          "end": 300.52,
          "en": "So both of the value binding and the input event listening,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 300.52,
          "end": 304.76,
          "en": "get rid of both and instead add a new directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.76,
          "end": 308.67,
          "en": "on the input, the v-model directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.67,
          "end": 312.95,
          "en": "And this v-model directive now simply wants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.95,
          "end": 316.69,
          "en": "the data property it should manage for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.69,
          "end": 319.78,
          "en": "so in our case, the name property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 319.78,
          "end": 323.22,
          "en": "The name property now is managed by Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 323.22,
          "end": 327.18,
          "en": "such that it's updated on the input event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.18,
          "end": 330.71,
          "en": "and the name properties value is then sent back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330.71,
          "end": 332.29,
          "en": "into the input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 332.29,
          "end": 337.29,
          "en": "So v-model is simply just a shortcut for v-bind value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 338.45,
          "end": 340.31,
          "en": "and v-on input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 340.31,
          "end": 342.637,
          "en": "v-model is just a shortcut for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 342.637,
          "end": 344.48,
          "en": "And if I now save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 344.48,
          "end": 346.85,
          "en": "we therefore get the same behavior as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.81,
          "end": 349.59000000000003,
          "en": "but with less code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 349.59000000000003,
          "end": 352.98,
          "en": "And this is a concept called two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.98,
          "end": 355.76,
          "en": "because we're communicating in both ways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.76,
          "end": 358.61,
          "en": "we are listening to an event coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 358.61,
          "end": 362.17,
          "en": "out of the input element you could say to the input event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.17,
          "end": 366.05,
          "en": "And at the same time, we're writing the value back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 366.05,
          "end": 369.75,
          "en": "to the input element through its value attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 369.75,
          "end": 371.9,
          "en": "through its value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 371.9,
          "end": 373.71,
          "en": "That's why it's called two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.71,
          "end": 376.63,
          "en": "because we communicate in both directions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 376.63,
          "end": 378.12,
          "en": "And this is useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.12,
          "end": 381.48,
          "en": "it makes getting user input and updating it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.48,
          "end": 383.17,
          "en": "much easier as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 383.17,
          "end": 385.76,
          "en": "it's less code and therefore absolutely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.76,
          "end": 389.28,
          "en": "a pattern and specifically a directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 389.28,
          "end": 390.48,
          "en": "you should keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
